{
  "_readme": "Reviewable curation rules for the 4-letter token pools. Edit freely and re-run filter.py. Alphabet is fixed by generate.py (consonants bdfghjklmnprstvwz, vowels aeiou; no c/q/x/y), so profanity written with 'c'/'y' cannot occur and is omitted. The profanity list is a STARTER set: it must be human-expanded, reviewed, and internationalized before it is used for a live namespace. Every substring rule is checked as a 'substring anywhere inside the token' (3-letter substrings also catch embedded profanity). Boundary (token1[3]+token2[0]) rules apply only inside scan.py, not to single tokens.",
